From: Local Z96A DTS verification
Subject: [PATCH] rk3568: z96a: enable the internal USB camera power rail

The internal Microdia/Sonix USB camera (0c45:6368) is behind the
GL852G hub and is powered from a GPIO2_D0 controlled rail.  The
vendor BSP device tree (z96a-camera-vcc) drives this rail high,
but the mainline Z96A device tree leaves the GPIO unconfigured, so
the camera never enumerates and uvcvideo has no device to bind to.

Add a fixed regulator for the camera rail and keep it enabled at
boot.  With the rail on, the camera shows up as a standard UVC
device and is driven by the in-tree uvcvideo driver.

Tested on Sunniwell Z96A Type-C: the camera enumerates as
2-1.2 0c45:6368 and produces 1920x1080 MJPG frames.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-sunniwell-z96a-typec.dts | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-sunniwell-z96a-typec.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-sunniwell-z96a-typec.dts
@@ -354,6 +354,21 @@
 		vin-supply = <&vcc5v0_sys>;
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The internal USB camera is powered from a GPIO-controlled rail.
+	 * Keep it enabled so uvcvideo sees the device (0c45:6368) at boot.
+	 */
+	vcc_camera: regulator-vcc-camera {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		enable-active-high;
+		gpio = <&gpio2 RK_PD0 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&camera_pwr_en>;
+		regulator-name = "vcc_camera";
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+	};
+
 	wifi_power: regulator-wifi-power {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
 		enable-active-high;
@@ -854,6 +869,9 @@
 		vcc5v0_usb_keyboard_en: vcc5v0-usb-keyboard-en {
 			rockchip,pins = <2 RK_PD7 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_none>;
 		};
+		camera_pwr_en: camera-pwr-en {
+			rockchip,pins = <2 RK_PD0 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_none>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	wireless-bluetooth {
